cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Open Health Sync in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Open Health Sync"
abstract: >-
  Open Health Sync is an open source, self-hosted health data aggregator. It collects data from
  wearables and health apps (Apple Health, Health Connect, Garmin, Oura, WHOOP, Fitbit, Withings,
  Polar, Strava, Dexcom and others) and serves it in one data model through a REST API, FHIR R4,
  Open mHealth, signed webhooks, CSV and Parquet exports and a read-only MCP server. It is one Go
  binary plus PostgreSQL.
authors:
  - name: "Open Health Sync contributors"
version: "0.3.0"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/soma-intelligence/open-health-sync"
url: "https://openhealthsync.com"
keywords:
  - health data
  - wearables
  - health data aggregator
  - self-hosted
  - fhir
  - open mhealth
  - apple health
  - health connect
  - mcp
